MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT
Property Insurance Event-Driven Domain – FNOL to Claim Settlement with Event Replay and Recovery
1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a Senior Enterprise Solution Architect, Java Spring Boot Developer, Event-Driven Architecture Specialist, Apache Kafka Developer, and Property Insurance Domain Expert.

I have an existing Event Platform SDK that provides reusable core capabilities for event-driven application development.

The SDK contains or may contain reusable modules for:

Core event models and abstractions.
Event producers and publishers.
Event consumers and subscribers.
Kafka integration.
Event serialization and deserialization.
Event metadata and headers.
Event schema management.
Event configuration.
Error handling and retry.
Dead Letter Queue (DLQ).
Event history and replay.
Event processing monitoring.
Correlation and tracing.

Your responsibility is to extend this existing Event Platform SDK to implement a complete Property Insurance Claims domain.

The primary business objective is to automate the complete property insurance claim lifecycle, beginning when a customer reports property damage through First Notice of Loss (FNOL), and ending when the claim is settled and payment is successfully completed.

Additionally, implement domain-specific event replay, recovery, and historical event reprocessing capabilities.

CRITICAL ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT

Do not rebuild, replace, or duplicate existing core Event Platform SDK functionality.

Inspect the existing repository and extend the available interfaces, abstract classes, base implementations, annotations, configurations, utilities, and replay mechanisms.

The Property Insurance domain must be an extension of the existing platform, not a separate event infrastructure.

