3. TARGET ARCHITECTURE

Implement three architectural layers.

Layer 1: Existing Core Event Platform SDK

Responsible for generic event infrastructure:

Event publishing.
Event consumption.
Event serialization.
Event deserialization.
Event metadata.
Kafka integration.
Schema validation.
Retry handling.
DLQ processing.
Event replay engine.
Event audit infrastructure.
Event tracing and monitoring.

Keep insurance-specific business rules out of this layer.

Layer 2: Property Insurance Domain SDK

Responsible for property insurance-specific event capabilities:

Property insurance domain models.
FNOL event models.
Policy event models.
Claim event models.
Adjuster event models.
Damage assessment event models.
Settlement event models.
Payment event models.
Domain-specific producers.
Domain-specific consumers.
Property insurance event payloads.
Insurance-specific replay policies.
Claim lifecycle validation.
Layer 3: Property Insurance Application

Responsible for business workflows:

FNOL submission.
Policy validation.
Claim creation.
Adjuster assignment.
Damage assessment.
Settlement calculation.
Claim approval.
Payment processing.
Claim settlement.
Customer notification.
Replay administration.

Ensure proper dependency inversion and separation of responsibilities.

