10. END-TO-END FNOL-TO-SETTLEMENT BUSINESS WORKFLOW

Implement the complete business workflow.

Step 1: FNOL submission

Customer reports property damage through mobile app, website, or call center.

FNOL Service:

Validate request.
Generate FNOL ID.
Store FNOL.
Publish FNOLSubmitted.
Step 2: Policy validation

Policy Service:

Validate policy status.
Check incident date against coverage period.
Validate insured property.
Verify coverage and exclusions.
Publish PolicyValidated or PolicyRejected.
Step 3: Claim creation

Claims Service:

Consume PolicyValidated.
Create claim.
Generate Claim ID.
Store claim.
Publish ClaimCreated.
Step 4: Adjuster assignment

Assignment Service:

Receive ClaimCreated.
Identify suitable adjuster.
Assign adjuster.
Publish AdjusterAssigned.
Step 5: Damage assessment

Assessment Service:

Receive assignment/assessment request.
Record inspection results.
Upload supporting documents.
Publish DamageAssessmentCompleted.
Step 6: Settlement calculation

Settlement Service:

Validate coverage.
Calculate covered loss.
Apply deductible.
Apply depreciation where relevant.
Apply policy limits and sublimits.
Calculate proposed settlement.
Publish SettlementCalculated.
Step 7: Approval

Approval Service:

Validate settlement.
Enforce approval authority.
Record approval decision.
Publish ClaimApproved or ClaimRejected.
Step 8: Payment

Payment Service:

Consume approved payment request.
Check payment idempotency.
Process payment through the configured payment integration.
Publish PaymentProcessed or PaymentFailed.
Step 9: Claim settlement

Claims Service:

Consume PaymentProcessed and applicable reconciliation confirmation.
Update claim status.
Record settlement.
Publish ClaimSettled.
Step 10: Customer notification

Notification Service:

Consume CustomerNotificationRequested.
Send email, SMS, or portal notification.
Record notification outcome.

Use configurable business rules and avoid assuming that every claim follows an identical straight-through workflow.

