PropertyInsuranceReplayService
ClaimEventReplayService
FnolEventReplayService
ReplayRequest
ReplayCriteria
ReplayExecution
ReplayResult
ReplayStatus
ReplayEventValidator
ReplayAuditService

Adapt naming and responsibilities to the existing SDK.

13.2 Replay scenarios
Scenario A: Single FNOL replay

A FNOL event was published, but claim creation did not complete because of a consumer defect.

Replay FNOLSubmitted and verify that policy validation and claim creation complete successfully.

Scenario B: Claim-level replay

Replay all events for a specific claim.

Example:

ClaimCreated → AdjusterAssigned → DamageAssessmentCompleted → SettlementCalculated → ClaimApproved → PaymentProcessed → ClaimSettled

Requirements:

Select by claimId.
Preserve original event ordering.
Validate event sequence.
Preserve original event references.
Prevent duplicate business operations.
Support pause and resume.
Scenario C: Date-range replay

Recover FNOL events affected by a system outage.

Support:

Start timestamp.
End timestamp.
Event type filtering.
Domain filtering.
Replay preview.
Execution summary.
Scenario D: DLQ replay

Recover failed events.

Requirements:

Select DLQ events by claim ID, event ID, and event type.
Validate the original payload.
Confirm the underlying failure is resolved.
Reprocess through the original domain consumer.
Track replay attempts.
Maintain failure history.
Scenario E: Consumer-version replay

A new Settlement Service version fixes a calculation defect.

Requirements:

Replay selected historical events using the new consumer version.
Preserve the original event data.
Support dry-run comparison.
Record consumer version.
Do not overwrite approved settlements automatically.
Require authorized business approval for recalculation.
Scenario F: Downstream outage recovery

Recover events affected by notification or external assessment system outages.

Replay only affected event types.

Do not replay unrelated business workflows.

Scenario G: Full claim lifecycle reconstruction

Reconstruct the event history and current claim projection using historical events.

Identify missing events, inconsistent transitions, and data discrepancies.

Do not repeat external financial side effects.

13.3 Replay modes

Implement:

DRY_RUN

Retrieve events.
Validate schemas.
Validate event ordering.
Identify duplicates.
Identify potential side effects.
Generate preview.
Do not change business state.

REPROCESS

Reprocess eligible historical events through appropriate domain consumers.
Apply idempotency.
Record execution results.
Protect external side effects.

RECOVERY

Reprocess previously failed events.
Use existing retry and DLQ mechanisms.

PROJECTION_REBUILD

Reconstruct read models from historical events.
Use an isolated rebuild target.
Do not modify authoritative financial records.
Support comparison and controlled replacement.
