If historical event ordering information is insufficient, flag the affected replay for validation or manual review.

14. CRITICAL PAYMENT AND FINANCIAL SAFETY

Replay must never cause duplicate financial transactions.

Implement:

Unique payment idempotency keys.
Payment transaction reference verification.
Authoritative payment status reconciliation.
Immutable financial audit history.
Protection against duplicate PaymentRequested processing.
Protection against repeated PaymentProcessed side effects.
Authorized settlement recalculation.
Separation of historical events from new business commands.
Notification deduplication.
Explicit claim state validation.

A replayed PaymentProcessed event should normally reconstruct or verify the payment state, not execute another payment.

A replayed PaymentRequested event must check the authoritative payment reference before initiating any external operation.

An approved claim must not have its settlement amount automatically overwritten during replay.

For failed payment processing, preserve the approved claim state until payment is reconciled.

