Event processing audit.

Ensure that events are not silently lost.

Ensure failed processing can be investigated and recovered.

Document any limitations in the existing platform's delivery guarantees.

16. BUSINESS VALIDATION RULES

Implement the following validations:

FNOL must reference a valid policy.
Policy must be active on the incident date.
Insured property must match the policy.
Incident date must satisfy policy terms.
Duplicate claims must be detected or flagged.
Claim amounts must be non-negative.
Assessment must be completed before settlement calculation.
Approval must precede payment.
Payment must not exceed the approved settlement.
Claim must not be marked settled before successful payment reconciliation.

Do not automatically reject claims that require further investigation.

Use configurable policy terms, exclusions, deductibles, limits, and settlement rules.

17. SECURITY AND AUDIT

Implement or reuse existing security mechanisms.

Requirements:

Secure administrative replay APIs.
Role-based access control.
Replay authorization.
Approval requirements for financial recalculation.
Sensitive data protection.
Encryption in transit and at rest.
Audit trail for business decisions.
Audit trail for replay requests and executions.
No unnecessary PII in event payloads or logs.
